WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.552
Hi! Today I'll show you my flat.

2
00:00:06.952 --> 00:00:11.664
Which rooms are there? What is it like?

3
00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:17.815
This is my flat. Listen:

4
00:00:18.215 --> 00:00:20.527
the living room

5
00:00:20.927 --> 00:00:23.311
the bedroom

6
00:00:23.711 --> 00:00:25.783
the kitchen

7
00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:28.255
the bathroom

8
00:00:28.655 --> 00:00:30.727
the hallway

9
00:00:31.127 --> 00:00:33.367
the garden

10
00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:39.731
What is there in the flat? Listen:

11
00:00:40.131 --> 00:00:42.971
There is a balcony.

12
00:00:43.371 --> 00:00:48.611
After es gibt comes the accusative: einen, eine, ein.

13
00:00:49.011 --> 00:00:51.875
There is no garden.

14
00:00:52.275 --> 00:00:54.347
What a pity!

15
00:00:56.033 --> 00:01:00.265
What is the flat like? Listen:

16
00:01:00.665 --> 00:01:03.409
The kitchen is big.

17
00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:05.545
But:

18
00:01:05.945 --> 00:01:08.689
The bathroom is small.

19
00:01:09.089 --> 00:01:14.257
More words: bright and dark, quiet and loud.

20
00:01:15.967 --> 00:01:20.415
In flat adverts you often see abbreviations:

21
00:01:20.815 --> 00:01:24.423
It means: two-room flat.

22
00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:30.413
Listen: Lena has a new flat.

23
00:01:30.813 --> 00:01:33.845
What's your new flat like?

24
00:01:34.245 --> 00:01:37.085
It's bright and quiet.

25
00:01:37.485 --> 00:01:40.349
How many rooms does it have?

26
00:01:40.749 --> 00:01:43.877
Two – and a balcony!

27
00:01:44.277 --> 00:01:47.957
Great! Is it expensive?

28
00:01:48.357 --> 00:01:51.557
No, it's affordable.

29
00:01:53.267 --> 00:02:01.507
Now you! Describe your flat. What is there? What is it like?

30
00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.336
Great! Now you can:

31
00:02:15.736 --> 00:02:20.544
You describe your flat: the rooms and what it's like.

32
00:02:20.944 --> 00:02:23.064
See you soon!
